OL,3,GNEWSACharity buildings from 17th
OL,4,ACentury to become 'affordable' homes
OL,5,Afor young people
OL,6,
OL,7,FA Grade-II listed building that once
OL,8,Fprovided charitable housing is set to
OL,9,Fbe converted into "affordable" homes
OL,10,Ffor young people.
OL,12,FPenmynydd Almshouses, on Anglesey, were
OL,13,Festablished in 1620 following a #1,000
OL,14,Fwill donation to supply housing for
OL,15,F"the poor of good and honest character"
OL,16,Fin the area.
OL,18,FTen men aged over 50 lived there
OL,19,Finitially, before women were later
OL,20,Fallowed to move in. By the 1960s, the
OL,21,Fnumber of units halved to five, and the
OL,22,Flast resident moved out in May 2011.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
